1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,664
Every conference season, social media lights
up: this lab has five NeurIPS papers,

2
00:00:05,664 --> 00:00:07,667
that group has three at ICML.

3
00:00:08,267 --> 00:00:09,740
The news is real.

4
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:12,600
But it only tells half the story.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,864
This video follows 26 lecturers and
researchers at universities and institutes in

6
00:00:21,864 --> 00:00:22,641
Vietnam,

7
00:00:22,641 --> 00:00:30,699
each with at least one paper accepted at
one of five top AI conferences since 2020:

8
00:00:30,699 --> 00:00:34,000
ICLR, NeurIPS, ICML, CVPR and ACL.

9
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:37,203
Only main-track papers count.

10
00:00:37,203 --> 00:00:42,049
The figures come from the
conferences' official lists,

11
00:00:42,049 --> 00:00:48,600
from OpenReview and from each person's
own page, as of 30 September 2026.

12
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,818
First, the rise is real.

13
00:00:53,818 --> 00:01:06,068
The group had 1 accepted paper in 2020,
7 in 2024, 24 in 2025 and 63 in 2026.

14
00:01:06,068 --> 00:01:11,000
NeurIPS and ICML lead the rise.

15
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:14,649
It is not just this group.

16
00:01:14,649 --> 00:01:24,381
Main-track NeurIPS papers with at least
one author at a Vietnamese institution went

17
00:01:24,381 --> 00:01:28,836
from 4 in 2020 to at least 30 in 2026,

18
00:01:28,836 --> 00:01:34,933
from 0.21% to 0.56% of all
papers at the conference.

19
00:01:35,533 --> 00:01:38,131
Two things to keep in mind.

20
00:01:38,131 --> 00:01:45,250
11 of the 63 papers from 2026 are so
far known only from personal pages or

21
00:01:45,250 --> 00:01:52,562
university announcements, because the
NeurIPS 2026 list is still incomplete.

22
00:01:52,562 --> 00:01:59,200
And 13 are by people who started
working in Vietnam in 2023 or later.

23
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:03,567
But announcements only
cover accepted papers.

24
00:02:03,567 --> 00:02:08,908
Of these five conferences, only ICLR
publishes every submission with its outcome,

25
00:02:08,908 --> 00:02:12,600
so it is the one place where
the other side can be seen.

26
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:17,799
The group sent 61 papers to ICLR.

27
00:02:17,799 --> 00:02:22,119
13 were accepted, which is 21%.

28
00:02:22,119 --> 00:02:27,693
The other 48 were rejected or withdrawn.

29
00:02:27,693 --> 00:02:37,867
For comparison, ICLR as a whole accepted
32.1% in 2025 and 27.4% in 2026.

30
00:02:38,467 --> 00:02:46,093
In other words, for every accepted
paper about 4.7 were submitted.

31
00:02:46,093 --> 00:02:55,800
Withdrawing is common too: at ICLR 2026,
5,042 of 19,525 submissions were withdrawn.

32
00:02:57,200 --> 00:03:02,305
The other four conferences do
not publish their rejections.

33
00:03:02,305 --> 00:03:09,054
If each person's acceptance rate there
is assumed to match their rate at ICLR,

34
00:03:09,054 --> 00:03:13,986
then 120 accepted papers stand
for about 385 submissions,

35
00:03:13,986 --> 00:03:17,533
about 3.2 submissions per accepted paper.

36
00:03:18,133 --> 00:03:20,002
This is only an estimate.

37
00:03:20,002 --> 00:03:25,534
Someone who never submitted to ICLR
counts as having no rejections at all,

38
00:03:25,534 --> 00:03:28,001
so the real figure may be higher.

39
00:03:28,001 --> 00:03:32,113
And a rejected paper is
usually revised and sent again:

40
00:03:32,113 --> 00:03:37,570
at least 5 papers rejected at ICLR
were later accepted at one of the five

41
00:03:37,570 --> 00:03:38,467
conferences.

42
00:03:39,867 --> 00:03:42,392
Who is on each paper?

43
00:03:42,392 --> 00:03:51,533
An accepted paper has 5.4 authors on
average: 2.6 in Vietnam and 2.7 abroad.

44
00:03:52,133 --> 00:03:58,763
64 of the 79 papers with known affiliations
have at least one co-author abroad.

45
00:03:58,763 --> 00:04:04,133
Working with groups abroad is not
the exception; it is the norm.

46
00:04:05,533 --> 00:04:09,870
The people with the most accepted
papers on the list are Khoa D.

47
00:04:09,870 --> 00:04:12,852
Doan, Ngo Van Linh,
Cuong Pham and Tuan Dam.

48
00:04:12,852 --> 00:04:17,867
Each person's record, including their
ICLR submissions, is on the website.

49
00:04:19,267 --> 00:04:25,872
So, is it easy to get a paper into a top
AI conference while working in Vietnam?

50
00:04:25,872 --> 00:04:28,680
The data says rejection is normal.

51
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:35,533
Each announced paper comes from several
submissions, several co-authors and, often,

52
00:04:35,533 --> 00:04:37,267
collaborators abroad.

53
00:04:37,867 --> 00:04:41,132
That does not make the
achievement smaller.

54
00:04:41,132 --> 00:04:43,867
It shows what the achievement takes.

55
00:04:44,467 --> 00:04:49,977
A few caveats: the people were picked by
hand and are not a representative sample.

56
00:04:49,977 --> 00:04:52,397
Rejections can be seen at ICLR only.

57
00:04:52,397 --> 00:04:55,959
And counting papers says
nothing about their quality.

58
00:04:55,959 --> 00:05:01,133
The method and the full figures are on
the website linked in the description.
